    "narrative": "The slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP is headlined by a trio of elite offensive projections, led by **Jose Caballero** (80.26), who benefits from a prime matchup against Abbott. **Caballero** is our strongest play, bolstered by an 18% skill advantage against the starter and a wind-aided park factor that maximizes his potential for both counting stats and stolen bases. Close behind is **Corbin Carroll** (79.53), whose matchup against Bradley is elevated by the target\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a green light for **Carroll**\u2019s elite sprint speed to exploit the base paths. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.57) round out our top-tier plays, both operating with significant platoon and park advantages that elevate their efficiency well into the \"Strong\" category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Zach McKinstry** on the bench. Despite a score of 42.06 and a favorable park adjustment, **McKinstry** ultimately fell short of the optimizer's threshold for a start, as his lower baseline compared to **Austin Riley** or the high-upside plays in the outfield forced him to the pine. We are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, most notably for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Josh Naylor**, **Max Muncy**, **Alex Freeland**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Corbin Carroll**. While our calculations assume standard placement, any significant drop in batting order for these players could compress their efficiency scores. Furthermore, while **Brice Turang** provides essential speed, he faces a tough assignment against Sale, forcing us to lean heavily on the favorable matchups for **Jose Caballero** and **Corbin Carroll** to secure the Roto categories today.",
